        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">Average technology\n\n# Included processes\nThis data set includes the material use for the manufacturing of the electronic installations in the residental building according to Klingler and Kasser, 2011. The source states that 95 % of the mass volume is accounted for, which covers about 100 individual components. 5 newly constructed multi-familiy residental buildings were taken into account. The connection to the public electricity grid was not taken into account. Only the basic equipment was accounted for (light in staircase and basement). The neon tubes and lamp fitting, as well as the control gear (EVG and VVG) were modelled with an energy saving light bulb. The electrical system has a life-span of 30 years. Transport is included.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
